    Return the length of the longest strictly increasing subsequence of nums. The solution must handle 10^5 elements in well under one second, so it needs O(n log n) time.

canonical_answer:
from bisect import bisect_left
def lis_length(nums):
    tails = []
    for x in nums:
        i = bisect_left(tails, x)
        if i == len(tails):
            tails.append(x)
        else:
            tails[i] = x
    return len(tails)

