def word_break(s: str, words: list[str]) -> bool:
    Return True if s can be split into a sequence of one or more words from words (each word may be reused). Return True for an empty s.

canonical_answer:
def word_break(s, words):
    ws = set(words)
    ok = [True] + [False] * len(s)
    for i in range(1, len(s) + 1):
        ok[i] = any(ok[j] and s[j:i] in ws for j in range(i))
    return ok[-1]

