Write a Python function that meets the following specification. Use only the Python standard library.

def regex_match(s: str, p: str) -> bool:
    Return True if pattern p matches the whole of s. In p, '.' matches any single character and '*' matches zero or more of the preceding element. Every '*' is preceded by a valid character or '.'. Do not use the re module.

canonical_answer:
def regex_match(s, p):
    from functools import lru_cache
    @lru_cache(None)
    def m(i, j):
        if j == len(p):
            return i == len(s)
        first = i < len(s) and p[j] in (s[i], ".")
        if j + 1 < len(p) and p[j + 1] == "*":
            return m(i, j + 2) or (first and m(i + 1, j))
        return first and m(i + 1, j + 1)
    return m(0, 0)

